.TH CCOL_R_MEMPOOL_DESTROY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
ccol_r_mempool_destroy \- destroy a ranged memory pool
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cmempool.h>

ccol_r_mempool_destroy(rmp);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Frees every resource of the ranged memory pool, every sub-pool included.
For a pool that was created from a preallocated buffer, this macro does
not free the buffer itself.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
rmp  Ranged memory pool to destroy. The macro sets it to NULL
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
It is safe to call this macro with a NULL pointer
For a preallocated pool, the caller owns the lifetime of the buffer

The macro evaluates rmp exactly once. It must be a modifiable lvalue,
such as a variable or an element of an array, so an expression with a
side effect, such as handles[i++], destroys and clears one element.
.fi
.SH WARNINGS
.nf
A pointer from the dynamic fallback that nobody freed causes an
assertion failure, so free every allocated entry before you destroy the
pool.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_r_mempool_create (3),
.BR ccol_mempool_destroy (3)
